  "report": "Implementation review passed; operator acceptance remains separate.\n\nRESULT: accepted\n\n**OBSERVED:** At base `9da64dbd`, the candidate checkpoint matches the four uncommitted Rust files; `git diff --check` exits 0. The changes stay within the approved allocation. The prior stale-comment finding is closed, the selection packet now names all four paths and copy-only state-root use, and DU-C02 now pins C collation.\n\n**Obligations:** RG-REQ-008, RG-REQ-011, RG-REQ-008-L01/L03/L04/L05/L06/L08, RG-REQ-011-L06, and P-DU-01/02/03 are **accepted within this slice’s stated boundary**. No finding or new decision remains.\n\n| Check | Review assessment |\n|---|---|\n| DU-C01 | **BUILDER-EXECUTED:** 126 doc-facts tests passed; names and assertions inspected. Not independently run. |\n| DU-C02 | **BUILDER-EXECUTED:** 1,289 rgr library, 6 CLI, and 3 overlay tests passed; the corrected two-file scope assertion passed. Not independently run. |\n| DU-C03 | **BUILDER-EXECUTED:** fmt and clippy passed. **EXECUTED:** `git diff --check` passed. |\n| DU-C04 | **BUILDER-EXECUTED:** isolated CLI proof. **OBSERVED:** captures show poco changing from exit 2 in both modes to a 15-document human listing and 16 JSON entries; the mode-000 document has `\"content_hash\": null`. The serving run was not independently repeated. |\n| DU-C05 | **BUILDER-EXECUTED:** cleanup check. **OBSERVED:** the operator registry digest matches the recorded before digest, and only manager-owned before-roots remain. |\n\n**OBSERVED witness:** `poco/packaging/README.txt:1` reads ` POCO C++ Libraries`; byte `0x92` occurs at offset 232. Its captured JSON hash matches the checkout’s SHA-256, `dae0857d…f86993`. **OBSERVED preservation example:** `leveldb/README.md:1` begins “LevelDB is a fast key-value storage library…”; the captured before/after human listings are byte-identical at `9 documents`, and their parsed JSON is equal.\n\nThe four paths each serve an allocated obligation: `doc-facts/src/lib.rs` hashes bytes before decoding and always serializes the hash key; `lib_tests.rs` checks readable, undecodable, and unreadable outcomes; `rgr/src/presentation/docs.rs` accepts a required key whose value may be null; `docs_tests.rs` checks decode and filtered JSON re-emission. `ContentRead` serves the existing inventory and extraction callers, distinguishing decoded text from bytes read but undecodable; a plain I/O error would lose that distinction. The required-nullable decoder serves the CLI wire field; a plain `Option` would also accept a missing key.\n\nThis restores the VISION’s documentation-discovery step without fabricating a hash for bytes the tool could not read. **NOT RUN independently:** Cargo suites or a live daemon proof in this read-only review environment. The whole-workspace, smoke, and dogfood gates remain the operator’s post-acceptance work; this verdict does not claim those gates passed."
